# AI Assistant Specification for cloudflare-dns-terraform

## Machine-Readable Artefacts

The `.machine_readable/` directory contains structured metadata required for automated reasoning and project introspection.

- `STATE.scm`: Current project state, milestones, and progress.
- `META.scm`: Architecture decisions, development methodology, and rationale.
- `ECOSYSTEM.scm`: Ecosystem placement, upstream/downstream relationships, and interoperability.
- `AGENTIC.scm`: AI agent interaction patterns, affordances, and constraints.
- `NEUROSYM.scm`: Neurosymbolic integration configuration and hybrid reasoning settings.
- `PLAYBOOK.scm`: Operational runbook, workflows, and incident procedures.

Additional artefact:

- `AI.a2ml`: AI Assistant behavioural and operational instructions.

## Repository Roots

- Local repository root: `/var/mnt/eclipse/repos/cloudflare-dns-terraform`
- Remote mapping: `https://github.com/hyperpolymath/cloudflare-dns-terraform`

## Project Purpose

This repository manages DNS records for all hyperpolymath domains using Terraform
and the Cloudflare provider. The primary data source is `domains.csv`, which lists
all managed domains and their configuration flags (mail, tunnel, SSH, GitHub Pages, etc.).

## Key Files

- `main.tf` - Core DNS record definitions
- `email-security.tf` - SPF, DKIM, DMARC, MTA-STS, TLS-RPT records
- `security-headers.tf` - Cloudflare Transform Rules for security headers
- `workers.tf` - Cloudflare Workers deployment
- `variables.tf` - Terraform variable declarations
- `domains.csv` - Domain configuration data (the single source of truth)
- `workers/*.js` - Cloudflare Worker scripts

## Security Requirements

- Do NOT commit terraform.tfvars (contains API tokens).
- Do NOT hardcode Cloudflare API tokens in source files.
- Use HTTPS only.
- Pin all dependencies by SHA.
- Include SPDX license headers in all files.
- License: PMPL-1.0-or-later
